{"response":{"docs":[{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBA_2044607","ontology_name":"oba","ontology_prefix":"OBA","short_form":"OBA_2044607","description":["The amount of a sterile alpha motif domain-containing protein 12 when measured in blood serum."],"label":"amount of sterile alpha motif domain-containing protein 12 in blood serum","obo_id":"OBA:2044607","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["blood serum sterile alpha motif domain-containing protein 12 amount","level of sterile alpha motif domain-containing protein 12 in blood serum","sterile alpha motif domain-containing protein 12 amount in blood serum"]},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D049291","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["Seromas"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_D049291","description":["Tumor-like sterile accumulation of serum in a tissue, organ, or cavity. It results from a tissue insult and is the product of tissue inflammation. It most commonly occurs following MASTECTOMY."],"label":"Seroma","obo_id":"mesh:D049291","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C29772","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C29772","description":["The serum of a healthy, unvaccinated adult horse.  Sera are lipid-extracted, dialyzed, sterilized, and filtered and may contain preservatives such as sodium azide.  Normal horse serum may be used as a blocking agent to reduce background from non-specific binding or as a negative control in immunoassays. (NCI04)"],"label":"Serum, Horse","obo_id":"NCIT:C29772","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["Normal Horse Serum","SERUM, HORSE","Serum, Horse"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C61105","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C61105","description":["A sterile non-pyrogenic suspension of microspheres of human serum albumin with the stable, high-molecular-weight fluorocarbon gas perflutren, used as a contrast enhancement agent for ultrasound procedures. Because the acoustic impedance of perflutren protein-type A microspheres is much lower than that of blood, impinging ultrasound waves are scattered and reflected at the microsphere-blood interface and may be visualized with ultrasound imaging. At the frequencies used in adult echocardiography (2-5 MHZ) the microspheres resonate, which further increases the extent of ultrasound scattering and reflection."],"label":"Perflutren Protein-Type A Microspheres","obo_id":"NCIT:C61105","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["Optison","Perflutren Protein-Type A Microspheres"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OCCO_29205600","ontology_name":"occo","ontology_prefix":"OCCO","short_form":"OCCO_29205600","description":["Perform medical tests in a laboratory environment for use in the treatment and diagnosis of diseases in animals. Prepare vaccines and serums for prevention of diseases. Prepare tissue samples, take blood samples, and execute laboratory tests, such as urinalysis and blood counts. Clean and sterilize instruments and materials and maintain equipment and machines. May assist a veterinarian during surgery."],"label":"veterinary technologist or technician","obo_id":"OCCO:29205600","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C80829","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C80829","description":["A sterile preparation of purified immunoglobulin G (IgG) derived from large pools of human plasma. Upon administration, octagam provides passive immunization by increasing the recipient\u0027s serum levels of circulating antibodies. IgG antibodies have multiple functions, including binding to and neutralizing bacterial toxins; opsonization of pathogens; activation of complement; and suppression of pathogenic cytokines and phagocytes through binding to CD5, interleukin-1a (IL-1a), interleukin 6 (IL-6), tumor necrosis factor-alpha (TNF-alpha), and T-cell receptors."],"label":"Human Immunoglobulin G","obo_id":"NCIT:C80829","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["Flebogamma DIF","Gammagard","Gamunex-C","HUMAN IMMUNOGLOBULIN G","Hizentra","Human IgG","Human Immunoglobulin G","Octagam","Privigen"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBA_2044607","ontology_name":"efo","ontology_prefix":"EFO","short_form":"OBA_2044607","description":["The amount of a sterile alpha motif domain-containing protein 12 when measured in blood serum."],"label":"amount of sterile alpha motif domain-containing protein 12 in blood serum","obo_id":"OBA:2044607","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["blood serum sterile alpha motif domain-containing protein 12 amount","level of sterile alpha motif domain-containing protein 12 in blood serum","sterile alpha motif domain-containing protein 12 amount in blood serum"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBA_2044607","ontology_name":"pride","ontology_prefix":"PRIDE","short_form":"OBA_2044607","description":[],"label":"amount of sterile alpha motif domain-containing protein 12 in blood serum","obo_id":"OBA:2044607","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["blood serum sterile alpha motif domain-containing protein 12 amount","level of sterile alpha motif domain-containing protein 12 in blood serum","sterile alpha motif domain-containing protein 12 amount in blood serum"]}],"numFound":8,"start":0},"responseHeader":{"QTime":0,"status":0},"facet_counts":{"facet_fields":{"ontologyPreferredPrefix":["NCIT","3","EFO","1","mesh","1","OBA","1","OCCO","1","PRIDE","1"],"isDefiningOntology":["true","6","false","2"],"ontologyId":["ncit","3","efo","1","mesh","1","oba","1","occo","1","pride","1"],"ontologyIri":["http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ncit.owl","3","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/oba.owl","1","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/occo.owl","1","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pride.owl","1","https://w3id.org/biopragmatics/resources/mesh/mesh.ofn","1","http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/efo.owl","1"],"isObsolete":["false","8"],"type":["class","8"]}}}